   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Neuromuscular Performance Thresholds to Support Player Development in a Professional Soccer Academy</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">Neuromuscular Performance Thresholds to Support Player Development in a Professional Soccer Academy</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <dc:subject>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>soccer; strength; talent development; reactive forces; athlete monitoring</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:subject>
   <dc:type>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>Text</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:type>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Purpose: We aimed to compare neuromuscular performance between academy soccer players (U-17</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">Purpose: We aimed to compare neuromuscular performance between academy soccer players (U-17</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">U-19</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">U-19</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and U-21 categories) and first-team players</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and U-21 categories) and first-team players</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and to establish neuromuscular performance thresholds associated with the first-team level. Methods: Ninety-four male players participated and were followed over two seasons. Neuromuscular performance was assessed using force-plate and force-sensing frame technologies</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and to establish neuromuscular performance thresholds associated with the first-team level. Methods: Ninety-four male players participated and were followed over two seasons. Neuromuscular performance was assessed using force-plate and force-sensing frame technologies</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">including isometric hip adduction and abduction</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">including isometric hip adduction and abduction</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Nordic hamstring exercise</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">Nordic hamstring exercise</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">countermovement jump (CMJ)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">countermovement jump (CMJ)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and isometric squat hold. Peak force</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and isometric squat hold. Peak force</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">eccentric and concentric peak force</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">eccentric and concentric peak force</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">rate of force development</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">rate of force development</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">impulse</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">impulse</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">modified reactive strength index (RSI-modified)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">modified reactive strength index (RSI-modified)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">dynamic strength index (DSI) and limb asymmetry were analyzed. Linear mixed models</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">dynamic strength index (DSI) and limb asymmetry were analyzed. Linear mixed models</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">binary logistic generalized estimating equations (GEE)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">binary logistic generalized estimating equations (GEE)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve analyses were performed. Results: The neuromuscular variables that best discriminated between soccer academy and first-team were maximal hip pull force (OR = 2.53</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve analyses were performed. Results: The neuromuscular variables that best discriminated between soccer academy and first-team were maximal hip pull force (OR = 2.53</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">p 0.001)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">p 0.001)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">concentric peak force (OR = 2.42</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">concentric peak force (OR = 2.42</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">p 0.001)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">p 0.001)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">eccentric peak force (OR = 1.31</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">eccentric peak force (OR = 1.31</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">p = 0.046)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">p = 0.046)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">modified RSI (OR = 2.00</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">modified RSI (OR = 2.00</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">p 0.001)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">p 0.001)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">RFD at 200 ms (OR = 1.46</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">RFD at 200 ms (OR = 1.46</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">p = 0.004)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">p = 0.004)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and DSI (OR = 2.13</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and DSI (OR = 2.13</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">p 0.001). ROC analysis identified practical cutoff values for maximal hip abduction force (442 N)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">p 0.001). ROC analysis identified practical cutoff values for maximal hip abduction force (442 N)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">maximal concentric and eccentric forces during the CMJ (1856 and 1804 N</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">maximal concentric and eccentric forces during the CMJ (1856 and 1804 N</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">respectively)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">respectively)</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">modified RSI (0.58 msâ»Â¹) and DSI (0.57). Conclusions: First-team players demonstrate superior neuromuscular performance to academy players. The identified cutoff values should be considered exploratory benchmarks for distinguishing current competitive levels and require external</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">modified RSI (0.58 msâ»Â¹) and DSI (0.57). Conclusions: First-team players demonstrate superior neuromuscular performance to academy players. The identified cutoff values should be considered exploratory benchmarks for distinguishing current competitive levels and require external</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">prospective validation in independent cohorts from other clubs before practical application.</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">prospective validation in independent cohorts from other clubs before practical application.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
